dership, hot temper, loner. Teamwork lacking.\n\nThus best overall likely C due to reliability and teamwork, despite communication difficulty. But communication difficulty is serious for long flights. However B also has communication issues (nasty remarks). A lacks reliability data. D lacks teamwork.\n\nWe need to decide provisional preference. We must weigh strengths vs weaknesses. For long-distance, reliability and teamwork are crucial. C is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere, which is strong. Communication difficulty could be mitigated? But we have no data on severity. Egocentric also a concern. Not willing to further education could affect long-term suitability.\n\nB handles stress well, conscientious, but communication negative.\n\nA has strong technical but unknown reliability.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall due to explicit reliability and positive crew atmosphere. The communication weakness is notable but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks. D's arrogance is also severe.\n\nThus I will provisionally prefer Candidate C.\n\nWe should note uncertainties: lack of data on stress handling for C, technical competence unknown, communication difficulty may be critical. Also lack of data on A's reliability and stress handling.\n\nWhat would change vote: evidence that A is reliable and handles stress, or that C's communication issues are severe, or that B's teamwork can improve, etc.\n\nNow produce public message."}
