nd teamwork are crucial. C's communication difficulty could be severe. B's nasty remarks also severe. Which is worse? Hard to decide. We need to weigh. Perhaps we should be undecided because we lack stress handling for C and teamwork for B. D has reliability and problem solving but poor teamwork. A has technical but unknown reliability and stress.\n\nThus we might be undecided. But we need to state a current preferred candidate. Could be Candidate B because stress handling is explicit and reliability is high, and technical skills are good. However teamwork issues are serious. C's communication difficulty also serious. Which is less severe? Possibly B's \"nasty remarks\" could be more detrimental than C's difficulty communicating ideas. But C also egocentric. Both are issues. However B's stress handling is a unique strength not present elsewhere. That may tip in B's favor. Also B's technical weather assessment is important for long flights. So maybe B is best overall despite teamwork issues. But we need to consider that B's teamwork weakness is explicit and severe. C's teamwork strength (positive atmosphere) may offset communication difficulty? Actually positive atmosphere suggests good teamwork, but difficulty communicating ideas contradicts. So mixed.\n\nGiven the uncertainties, I think we should be cautious and vote Undecided, stating we need more info on stress handling for C and teamwork for B, also technical for C, etc. The instruction says if cannot yet choose, vote Undecided. We have conflicting evidence. So we can vote Undecided.\n\nThus produce public message: state current position Undecided, summarize evidence, alternatives, tradeoffs, uncertainties, what would change vote.\n\nProceed."}
